From: Ahrion Gallegos <ahrionmgallegos@gmail.com>
Subject: quectel-5g-tools: drop the ModemManager dependency + watchdog

This fork's modem stack is QModem + the Quectel vendor pcie_mhi
driver; ModemManager is not in the image at all. quectel-5g-tools'
Makefile hard-depends on +modemmanager, which silently pulls MM (and
its dbus/glib2/libmbim tail) back into every build - defeating the
stack swap.

The only piece of quectel-5g-tools tied to ModemManager is 5g-watchdog
(its recovery path). Everything else - 5g-info, 5g-monitor, 5g-lock,
5g-cell-lock, 5g-led-bars, quectel-at, modem-debug, the Prometheus
collectors - talks raw AT to /dev/ttyUSB2 and works fine without MM.

So: drop +modemmanager from DEPENDS and stop installing the
5g-watchdog binary + init script (it would just crash-loop without
MM). Session recovery is quectel-CM's job under QModem. 5g-cell-lock
(an AT-based cell-lock service vjt added upstream) is kept - it has no
MM dependency. The /etc/modemmanager/ignore-tty file still gets
installed; it's inert without MM and not worth a bigger diff.

Regenerated 2026-09-05 against quectel-5g-tools master
e709ca45ba75c242bc168f9ae4808a798bb0f9c9, which custom-feeds.txt now
pins. A prior version tracked the moving master branch and drifted:
upstream added the 5g-cell-lock init line, breaking hunk #3. Applied
by prepare.sh against the .build-deps/ checkout. If it stops applying,
bump the pin and refresh the hunks.

